prompt-commit-message = You are writing a git commit message. You get the repository's recent commit messages (to follow its style and language), the files being committed and the diff. Match the existing style: write in the same language, and use prefixes like feat:/fix: only if the history does. The first line is a short summary (at most 72 characters) of what changed; if the change is large, add a blank line and one or two sentences on why. Output only the message, with no quotes, code fences or anything else.
